      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_42",
      "quote": "Several sensitivity analyses were performed to evaluate the robustness of the pooled effect. Leave-one-out analysis demonstrated that removal of any single study produced only modest fluctuations in the magnitude of the pooled SMD and did not alter the direction of the effect, indicating that no individual trial disproportionately influenced the results. Similarly, analyses excluding studies with higher risk-of-bias ratings yielded effect estimates consistent with the primary analysis, suggesting that methodological quality alone did not drive the observed variability. Re-synthesizing the data using alternative estimators-including fixed-effect, DerSimonianLaird, and Hartung-Knapp-adjusted random-effects models-produced convergent results, further supporting analytic stability. Restricting the analysis to trials employing more standardized outcome assessment scales did not materially change the pooled estimate.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly reports multiple sensitivity analyses (leave-one-out, excluding higher risk-of-bias studies, alternative estimators, restricting to standardized scales) and describes their results."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_20d_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_42",
      "quote": "Taken together, these sensitivity analyses reinforce the directional robustness of the findings while acknowledging the inherent limitations imposed by the small evidence base.",
